Notebook[{
Cell["Deconvolving Biological Networks", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"df0514c6-cdbf-495b-acdd-95d54f76a17a"],

Cell["\<\
Recovering gene-regulatory Boolean networks from their behaviour\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"95281b2b-6704-417b-bca5-2ee3d89d4996"],

Cell["\<\
The algorithmic-information causal calculus of Zenil and colleagues applies \
its perturbation analysis to biological networks but reconstructs only \
cellular automata, never the biological networks themselves. Here the \
index-set deconvolution recovers real gene-regulatory Boolean networks \
exactly from their output repertoire. The models are the fission yeast cell \
cycle, the IRMA synthetic yeast circuit, the WNT5A melanoma network, myeloid \
differentiation and apoptosis, taken from the PyBoolNet collection.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3d1c0d6e-d64f-4acb-9441-6ab435bfc43c"],

Cell["The regulatory (activator/inhibitor) gate", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6d4a71fb-7cc6-43cf-a939-c61d0bda5ef0"],

Cell["\<\
Real regulatory logic is dominated by conjunctions: a gene is expressed when \
its activators are present and its repressors are absent. The \
single-repressor case is the named gate NIMPLIES and the all-repressor case \
is NOR, but the mixed multi-input case has no classical name. We add the \
REGULATORY gate for it, defined as the product of the activator literals and \
the negated inhibitor literals, out = (product over activators of v) times \
(product over inhibitors of (1 - v)). Its index-set signature is a reduced \
truth table with a single 1, whose position encodes the activator and \
inhibitor split. It generalises AND (all activators) and NOR (all inhibitors) \
and names the mixed conjunctions that pervade the models below.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"65c1bc43-eb42-4358-a0fe-7de4428e9491"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"5b0aa0cf-a5c8-401c-93de-5c962be640b7"],

Cell["\<\
(* Load the forward method, the deconvolution and its extensions, and the
   biological demonstration library, relative to this notebook. *)
nbDir = NotebookDirectory[];
idDir = ParentDirectory[nbDir];
root  = ParentDirectory[idDir];
Get[FileNameJoin[{root, \"papers\", \"method\", \"code\", \"lib\", \
\"CausalBoolCore.wl\"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{idDir, \"src\", \"Deconvolution.wl\"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{idDir, \"src\", \"CADeconvolution.wl\"}]];
Get[FileNameJoin[{nbDir, \"BioDemoLibrary.wl\"}]];
biocasesPath = FileNameJoin[{idDir, \"crosscheck\", \"bio_cases.json\"}];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"395ec5e6-b934-4927-a98a-513f093a3348"],

Cell["Deconvolve the biological networks", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e1a81fbf-9415-4940-9aae-1ffddd749bdd"],

Cell["\<\
(* Deconvolve each biological network from its output repertoire alone and
   confirm the recovered network reproduces the repertoire exactly.  The
   REGULATORY column counts the activator/inhibitor conjunctions named by the
   new gate. *)
bioPass = RunBioDemo[biocasesPath];\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"be14f9b5-ad69-458b-9e6e-2e03d94b3ca9"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"14.2 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (December 26, 2024)",
StyleDefinitions->"Default.nb",
ExpressionUUID->"fdf6f78d-5630-49f5-b499-067109ec007b"
]
